```yaml
spec:
  grid: 4-10 rows x 5-10 cols, black background
  red_markers:
    count: 1-3
    role: centers of 3x3 blue halo stamps
    pairwise_chebyshev_dist: >=3 so halos never overlap [observed]
    placement: interior or edge; 0-1 on grid edge per example [observed]
  other_fg_pixels:
    count: 0-3 single-pixel distractors
    colors: any except black(0), blue(1), red(2)
    min_chebyshev_dist_to_any_red: >=2 so they never fall inside a halo [observed]
  transform: |
    For each red pixel, fill every black cell in its 3x3 Chebyshev neighborhood with blue.
    Red pixels and other foreground pixels are preserved unchanged.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (simple forward transform)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H in [4,10], W in [5,10].
    2. Pick N_red in [1,3]. Place red pixels one at a time, each with Chebyshev distance >=3 from all previously placed reds (retry if needed; grid is large relative to count so acceptance is high).
    3. Pick N_distractor in [0,3]. For each, choose a random color from {3,4,5,6,7,8,9}, place at a random black cell with Chebyshev distance >=2 from every red pixel.
    4. Output = run the solver transform (expand each red into a clipped 3x3 blue halo on black cells).
```
